    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-09-08",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Peace Officer Standards and Training Agency Information Access Clarification Act</strong></p><p>This bill authorizes a new type of entity\u2014peace officer standards and training agencies\u2014to access criminal history record information maintained by the Federal Bureau of Investigation. The term <em>peace officer standards and training agency</em> means an agency of a state, the District of Columbia, or a U.S. territory that is authorized to set standards for the hiring, training, ethical conduct, and retention of its law enforcement officers through certification, licensing, or other similar qualification processes.&nbsp;</p>",
        "update_date": "2026-05-19T15:54:23Z"
      }
    ]
